      "text": "#TBT Michiganders have been using the Mackinac bridge to travel across the Straits of Mackinac, a body of water connecting Lake Michigan and Lake Huron, since 1957. The Mackinac Bridge is the longest suspension bridge between anchorages in the Western Hemisphere that connects the Upper and Lower peninsulas of Michigan. The \"Mighty Mac\" is located in the Sault Ste. Marie Station's Area of Responsibility. It is believed that the Sault Ste. Marie Station was first activated in July of 1924 in conjunction with the creation of the #BorderPatrol.\n\n#DetroitSector",
